   "line": 6,
   "text": "Why does every tone come out as itself? The route adds three copies of the input: fresh, one sample old, two samples old. Draw each as an arrow scaled by its weight, and add them tip to tail. As the wheel turns, all three arrows turn together, so their sum turns at the same speed. No new tone can appear.",
