  {
   "line": 7,
   "text": "Now sweep the tone from zero to four thousand hertz. Zero keeps one hundred percent. Two thousand keeps seventy. Four thousand, only forty. Gain and phase, for every tone: that's the frequency response. [surprise-oh] And there's the wall. Vowels live low and walk through. The edges of consonants live near three thousand, where the route keeps less than half.",
   "clip": "/Users/cleiton.loiola/personal/lessons/dsp-oppenheim/03-frequency-response/4-video/vo/line07.wav",
   "at": 78.23,
